{
 "id": "2026-10-25-four-corners-record-flood",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "New Mexico's San Juan River just broke a record from nineteen oh nine. Who is in its path?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "At Farmington, the river reached fourteen point one feet on Friday, the National Weather Service says. The old record, set in nineteen oh nine, was twelve point three. Days of heavy rain, over five inches in places, sent water off Colorado's mountains into the desert."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Authorities estimate about fifteen hundred homes and buildings were affected, based on a National Weather Service database. Rescuers pulled people from rooftops. Near Shiprock, the river passed its flood stage of fifteen point five feet, and hundreds of homes lost power."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "The Associated Press says more rain is expected through the weekend. As of Saturday, no deaths had been reported in either state. Farmington's police chief said, quote, this is not over."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the Four Corners see more flooding this week? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
